# Cursor Execution Harness (Frontend)

**Canonical:** [`../CLAUDE.md`](../CLAUDE.md) · **Frontend scope:** [`CLAUDE.md`](CLAUDE.md).

> **`docs/DevOps/Frontend/REACT_RULES.md`** is mandatory for UI work.

---

## Before `frontend/` changes

1. [`../CLAUDE.md`](../CLAUDE.md) — blueprint + agent behavior
2. [`CLAUDE.md`](CLAUDE.md) — layout, API integration
3. [`docs/DevOps/Frontend/REACT_RULES.md`](../docs/DevOps/Frontend/REACT_RULES.md) — React patterns (full rules)

If the page maps to a backend domain, read that app's doc (e.g. [`../backend/apps/titanic/_docs/CLAUDE.md`](../backend/apps/titanic/_docs/CLAUDE.md)).

---

## Quick rules

| Item | Rule |
|------|------|
| Routes | `app/**/page.tsx` |
| API helpers | `lib/*-api.ts` |
| State | One object per related UI state — avoid field-per-`useState` |
| Forms | `FormData`; capture `form = e.currentTarget` before `await` |
| Errors | Inline UI — no `alert()` |
| Backend | `http://127.0.0.1:8000`; Titanic uses `/titanic/*` (no extra `/api` prefix) |

